.TH MPQ 1 "2026-11-26" "mpq-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mpq \- inspect MoPaQ archives and extract their members
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpq
.RI [ "GLOBAL OPTIONS" "] info [\-\-] " "ARCHIVE" " [" "ARCHIVE ..." ]
.br
.B mpq
.RI [ "GLOBAL OPTIONS" "] list [\-i " "INDEX" " ...] [\-\-] " "ARCHIVE"
.br
.B mpq
.RI [ "GLOBAL OPTIONS" "] extract [\-i " "INDEX" " ...] [\-\-] " "ARCHIVE"
.br
.B mpq
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-v ", " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mpq info
displays archive information for one or more archives in operand order.
It continues after an individual archive fails.
.PP
.B mpq list
lists members of one archive.
.B mpq extract
extracts members of one archive to the current directory.
Both stop at the first operation failure.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options precede the command.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display global help. Use as a standalone request.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the mpq-tools and libmpq versions. Use as a standalone request.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress successful extraction notices. Requested data and errors remain visible.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Report operation and selection details on standard error.
Quiet and verbose are mutually exclusive.
.SH COMMAND OPTIONS
Place command options before the first archive operand.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command help. Use as the sole token after the command.
.TP
.BI "\-i " INDEX
.TQ
.BI "\-\-index " INDEX
.TQ
.BI \-\-index= INDEX
Select a zero-based member index for list or extract.
Repeat the option to process members in the given order, including duplicates.
Omit indexes to process all members in archive order.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat subsequent tokens as literal archive operands.
This marker is recognized in command scope before the first archive operand.
.SH EXTRACTION
Generated output names begin at
.BR file000000.xxx .
Members stream through temporary files in the destination directory.
A completed member replaces an existing file with the same generated name.
Failures before publication preserve any existing destination.
Earlier published members remain after a later member fails.
.PP
Ordinary extraction uses applicable libmpq sector integrity checks during
streaming. It does not perform an additional whole-member CRC32 or MD5
verification pass.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An operation or resource failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid invocation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mpq info archive.mpq
mpq list archive.mpq
mpq extract \-i 0 \-i 2 archive.mpq
.fi
.SH MIGRATION
Use
.B mpq info
in place of
.BR mpq-info ,
and
.B mpq list
or
.B mpq extract
in place of
.B mpq-extract
with its respective operation switch.
Subtract one from each legacy member number and pass it with
.BR \-i .
